        "created_at": "2011-08-08T18:29:24.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Several people on the boards and at Gen Con mentioned forced deployment, so I figured I’d make a quick post about it since it is one of my favorite cards (in the sense that it is thrilling to play against).</p>\n<p>One question that came up at Gen Con was how this card interacts with Voss’ alternate win condition, so I made a <a href=\"http://greaterthangames.info/forum/index.php/topic,12.0.html\" data-bbcode=\"true\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">post</a> about that over in Official Rulings.  However, we were also talking about how Forced Deployment is much easier to deal with if a hero can destroy it <em>before</em> it destroys itself at the start of the Villain turn.  That way, the heroes get to take shots at the minions before all of their “end of turn” effects trigger.</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:34:34.729Z",
